  "lineage": "Cross-cultural instrumental meditation recordings combine selected acoustic timbres and studio atmosphere. Deuter’s Koyasan explicitly credits erhu, shakuhachi, tamboura and Tibetan bowls with keyboards; Nawang Khechog’s Tibetan Meditation Music combines flute with chant and sparse accents. The default models the former palette without presenting it as the traditional ensemble of any single culture.",
